diff --git a/RELEASE.md b/RELEASE.md
index 3d791d5..a8a1990 100644
--- a/RELEASE.md
+++ b/RELEASE.md
@@ -1,5 +1,19 @@
 | Date       | Version | Comment                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
 |------------|---------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
+|            | Unreleased | 1. Breaking: KeltnerChannel accessors return their own series names instead of names borrowed from Bollinger and Donchian: `kc_mband` (was `mavg`), `kc_wband` (was `bbiwband`), `kc_pband` (was `bbipband`), `kc_hband_indicator` (was `dcihband`) and `kc_lband_indicator` (was `dcilband`). Code selecting a column by `Series.name` needs updating. |
+|            |         | 2. Breaking: `EMAIndicator` defaults `window` to 12, matching its `ema_indicator` delegate, `SMAIndicator` and `sma_indicator`, and its series is named `ema_12`. Callers passing `window` explicitly are unaffected, as is `add_all_ta_features`, which passes every window by name.                                                                    |
+|            |         | 3. Breaking: `SMAIndicator` defaults `window` to 12. Constructing it without a window previously raised `TypeError`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
+|            |         | 4. Breaking: `donchian_channel_mband`, `donchian_channel_wband` and `donchian_channel_pband` default `window` to 20, matching `DonchianChannel` and the hband and lband delegates, which restores the middle band to the midpoint of the channel those defaults produce.                                                                                 |
+|            |         | 5. Breaking: a period argument of 0 or less raises `ValueError` naming the parameter and the value, across all 67 period arguments. `RSIIndicator(close, window=0)` previously raised `ZeroDivisionError`.                                                                                                                                               |
+|            |         | 6. Fixed: ATR and ADX report warm-up rows as undefined rather than 0.0, which was indistinguishable from a flat market's genuine zero. `average_true_range` is NaN for `window - 1` rows, `adx_pos` and `adx_neg` for `window + 1`, and `adx` for `2 * window - 1`. `fillna=True` fills them as before.                                                  |
+|            |         | 7. Fixed: the three Keltner bands share one warm-up, so no outer band is computed from a partial window while the centreline is still undefined, and `keltner_channel_pband` returns NaN instead of `-inf` where the bands coincide.                                                                                                                     |
+|            |         | 8. Fixed: look-ahead bias removed from TRIX, KST, DPO, Vortex, KAMA and the Ichimoku spans under `visual=True`, each of which seeded warm-up rows from a series mean or a wrapping roll and so read future data into the past.                                                                                                                           |
+|            |         | 9. Fixed: On Balance Volume follows the three-way rule of the definitions it cites, so an unchanged close leaves the running total alone and the first bar contributes nothing.                                                                                                                                                                          |
+|            |         | 10. Fixed: Aroon resolves a tied extreme to the most recent bar rather than the earliest, as the definition requires. This changes `aroon_up` on 21.3 per cent of 19975 rows of the shipped data at window 25.                                                                                                                                           |
+|            |         | 11. Fixed: PSAR clamps the stop against both prior bars rather than only the older one, so it no longer publishes a stop on the wrong side of a price that has already traded.                                                                                                                                                                          |
+|            |         | 12. Fixed: indicators accept integer and nullable price dtypes (`int64`, `int32`, `Int64`, `Float64`), which previously raised `TypeError`.                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
+|            |         | 13. Fixed: empty and very short frames no longer raise `IndexError`; every indicator returns empty or NaN output instead.                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
+|            |         | 14. Performance: Ulcer Index and MFI replaced per-window Python callbacks with rolling aggregations, and WMA stopped rebuilding its weight vector on every window. Measured on 20000 rows at 26x, 57x and 28x, with output unchanged. CCI and Aroon keep their callbacks deliberately: the vectorized form is exact and faster but peaks at 320 MB and 216 MB on a million rows. |
 | 2023/11/02 | 0.11.0  | Fixing Volume Price Trend indicator [PR](https://github.com/bukosabino/ta/pull/311)                                                                                                                                                                             |
 | 2023/10/29 | 0.10.3  | Fixing Aroon indicator [PR](https://github.com/bukosabino/ta/pull/316); Fixing future warnings; Improving documentation [PR](https://github.com/bukosabino/ta/pull/318); Fix future data leakage [PR](https://github.com/bukosabino/ta/pull/324)                |
 | 2022/08/23 | 0.10.2  | Fixing bug on KAMA indicator https://github.com/bukosabino/ta/pull/303                                                                                                                                                                                          |
